a 16 year old pregnant girl in florida  will not be able to get an abortion  because a court has decided that she is  not sufficiently mature enough to decide  for herself whether it's the right  decision to carry the fetus to term or  to get an abortion this is absolute  madness the girl's name is not being  provided as she is under 18 and they  want to protect her identity but florida  has a new 15-week abortion ban the  constitutionality of which is being  questioned but it's staying in place for  now at least the state brought that  threshold down from the 24 weeks back  a couple months ago and there is a state  law in florida that requires minors to  get parental consent for an abortion  which i would argue should not be  necessary because  even though you're a minor it's still  your body after all it's still going to  be a decision that involves you for the  next 18 years plus so it seems like they  only have this rule in place as a way to  embarrass the girl who becomes pregnant  to have to have her go to her parents  and explain the situation that she's in  and try to get their approval but as it  pertains to this story the girl in  question could not get her parental  consent because she is parentless and  she lives with a relative and has an  appointed guardian but that wasn't good  enough for a circuit court judge who  denied the parental consent waiver and a  three-judge panel upheld the decision a  statement from the appeals court said  the appellant had not established by  clear and convincing evidence that she  was sufficiently mature to decide  whether to terminate her pregnancy so  per the state of florida the girl is not  mature enough to decide whether an  abortion makes sense for her yet she is  somehow mature enough to carry a baby to  term give birth and raise it to  adulthood how does that make any sense  at all  something tells me that being a parent  requires a lot more maturity than  deciding whether a medical procedure for  someone in your position makes sense for  you so this is just the latest example  of republican barbarity on the topic  like in the lead up to roe versus wade  getting overturned when we could kind of  see the writing on the wall because of  trump's supreme court justices and then  when the draft opinion was leaked and  then when it was made official back in  june all along the right wing assured  the rest of the country that they were  going to be responsible on this abortion  issue if roe got overturned that they  would not be completely draconian and  how they addressed the matter  and they would say things like oh we'll  have exceptions for rape well now that's  being put into question because they  realized how logistically challenging  that would be because it could easily  lead to an increase in false rape  accusations then they'd say things like  oh well there'll be exceptions for life  of the mother when the life the mother  is put at risk you'll be able to get an  abortion in that instance but now  they're realizing that you can't always  assess risk levels in this way where  it's like a hundred percent that the  mother's going to survive if she has the  child or 100 chance that she's going to  die if she has a child like usually it's  in this gray area where you don't know  with any certainty what's going to  happen so who's going to decide whether  or not you fit under that exception for  life of the mother and they also used to  say oh well if roe vs wade gets  overturned then you're going to be able  to travel to a different state to get an  abortion if it's illegal in your state  now we're starting to see states try to  criminalize that very practice as well  so the reality has been a lot more  draconian than many of us could have  even imagined and if there's any silver  lining at all in the horrors that these  countless women have had to deal with  across the country including in this  story  it's that maybe it will incentivize  people to go out and vote in the fa